            "typeName": "dsDescription",
            "multiple": true,
            "typeClass": "compound",
            "value": [
              {
                "dsDescriptionValue": {
                  "typeName": "dsDescriptionValue",
                  "multiple": false,
                  "typeClass": "primitive",
                  "value": "This dataset contains raw data from a study, \"Digits-in-Noise test implementations for onsite and online testing with normal-hearing adults.\" Data were collected from 30 normal-hearing adults in a controlled onsite session, with a subset of 22 participants completing the online version.\n\nThe study systematically investigates the effects of three key parameters on Speech Reception Thresholds (SRTs):\n1) Sound Presentation: Comparing Diotic vs. Dichotic (Antiphasic) presentation.\n2) Mixing Method: Comparing Fixed-speech, Fixed-noise, and Fixed-level (onsite only) approaches.\n3) Starting SNR: Assessing the impact of \"high\" (0 dB) vs. \"low\" (-16 dB) starting Signal-to-Noise Ratios.\n\nThe dataset includes trial-by-trial logs stored in JSON format for onsite tests and CSV format for online tests, following the open generic DIN test specification. These data support the findings published in Türüdü et al. (2025) in Acta Acustica."
                }
              }
            ]
          },
